hyprcrt - third-party notices

The tube model (energy-conserving scanlines with a brightness-dependent beam,
phosphor mask with the mean folded back to one, halation, afterglow, curved
glass) is the author's own, first written for an-earlier-project (src/platform/sdl2/crt.c)
and ported to GPU passes for an-earlier-project. Both MIT, (c) 2026 Dan Expo.

The screen warp, the exp2(hard * d^2) beam spot and the light/dark phosphor
mask multipliers follow the public-domain CRT shader by Timothy Lottes:
  "PUBLIC DOMAIN CRT STYLED SCAN-LINE SHADER by Timothy Lottes ...
   Please take and use, change, or whatever."

